# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Without this file the context is ~157 MB, nearly all of it the dashboard's
# node_modules, and it is sent to the daemon on every build of every service
# including the Go ones that have no use for it. Two entries below are not
# about size at all:
#
#   .env / .env.prod  `COPY . .` in the Go images puts them in a build layer.
#                     They never reach the published image, which copies out
#                     only the binary, but they sit in the build cache and in
#                     `docker build --target build`.
#
#   node_modules      dashboard.Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and then copies the
#   *.tsbuildinfo     source in. Whatever the host has would land on top of
#                     the install, and a stale tsbuildinfo makes `tsc -b`
#                     believe the project is current and skip the type-check.
#
# Kept on purpose: go.mod, go.sum, apps/, internal/, examples/, deployments/,
# the root index.html the landing page is built from, and migrations/, whose
# .sql files are embedded into the binaries (migrations/migrations.go).

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitattributes
.github
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
*.iml

# Dependencies, installed inside the image instead
**/node_modules

# Build output and incremental state
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
/bin
/out
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage.out

# Local tooling that no image builds from
Makefile
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# Documentation
*.md
docs
LICENSE
